# AgentDB context

Read **CLAUDE.md** at the project root for full context, commands, and conventions.

## Where to change what

| Change | Location |
|--------|----------|
| DB schema, VirtualFS, KV, overlay, audit | `src/agentdb/db/` |
| Service graph, tick loop, events, evaluator | `src/agentdb/simulation/` |
| Agent configs, CityTools, swarm build, runner | `src/agentdb/agents/` |
| Env config, default service code / seeding | `src/agentdb/config.py`, `src/agentdb/seed.py` |
| App wiring (DB, engine, swarm, FastAPI) | `main.py` |
| WebSocket broadcast, API, static UI | `src/agentdb/dashboard/` |

## Conventions

- Paths used by agents must be under `/city/` (CityTools validates).
- Service contract: `handle_load(load, config)` in `/city/services/<name>/main.py`.
- Use `CityTools.set_current_agent(name)` before dispatching so audit and events are attributed.
- Tests: `conftest.py` provides `db`; async tests use `async def` (pytest-asyncio).

Specs and implementation plans: `docs/superpowers/specs/`, `docs/superpowers/plans/`.
